      "message": "We have a kind of test in Chrome called a nocompile test that proves that certain bad forms won\u0027t pass the compiler.  I was trying to write one for the mismatched enum case here, but we don\u0027t have the infrastructure copied over from Chrome to do so.  So what I ask is that you try something locally like\n\nenum A { kA1, kA2 };\nenum B ( kB1, kB2 };\n\nMask\u003cA\u003e(kA1, kB2);\n\nand double-check that compilation breaks because of no matching template. Once you\u0027ve done that, you\u0027re good to go.",
